      "stageRecord": "The proper name 太郎 and the common noun 本 project NPs. Each NP combines with a following case head inside a head-final KP: が is the nominative exponent and を the accusative exponent. The verbal material 読 and ん forms one complex V head; ん is analyzed as the nasal-onbin component of the stem 読ん rather than as an independent argument-taking head. The final だ is selected as the overt finite past T head. Every supplied token is therefore associated with an ordinary pronounced terminal. The ideographic full stop in the displayed sentence is an orthographic delimiter and is not part of the supplied token list, so it is not introduced into the syntactic workspace.",
