      "stageRecord": "The VP merges to the left of the finite past head だ, yielding the head-final T′ order VP–T that directly produces 読んだ at the right edge. The subject is deliberately still shown in Spec-VP: this intermediate workspace establishes T before any movement from the already represented VP-internal position. Finite T carries an EPP requirement and nominative-Case licensing capacity, so the closest eligible nominal, 太郎が, is the prospective mover. Its nominative particle is present but is not yet licensed in the Spec-TP configuration.",
