      "stageRecord": "The subject KP moves from Spec-VP to the newly projected Spec-TP position. The derivation is represented with copies: the higher occurrence is pronounced and bears the input indices for 太郎 and が, while the original VP-internal occurrence remains structurally present but is silent. The two occurrences share lineage, and the higher one c-commands the lower one. Finite T licenses nominative Case on the raised KP in the Spec-head domain and thereby satisfies its EPP requirement. The lower copy remains the position to which the Agent theta-role was assigned, so the A-chain has one theta-position and one Case position without violating the Theta Criterion.",
