      "stageRecord": "The completed TP merges as the complement of a silent head-final declarative C. No further overt movement is required. The pronounced terminal sequence is exactly 太郎, が, 本, を, 読, ん, だ; the lower subject copy and declarative C are silent. The derivation converges in Government and Binding terms: the verb's Agent and Theme roles are each assigned once, the overt object is accusative-licensed under verbal government, the raised subject is nominative-licensed by finite T, the EPP is met, and the silent lower A-copy is bound by its c-commanding antecedent.",
